# Agent onboarding (services)

Before writing or changing code under `services/`, read its rules and docs into
context and follow them:

- Root `AGENTS.md` (services section) and `services/*/spec.md` — the twelve
  binaries, build/versioning, and subprocess + JSON-RPC conventions.
- `.cursor/rules/*` — monorepo rules (especially `service-contracts.mdc` and
  `services-change-propagation.mdc`).
- The touched module's `README.md` and `spec.md`. `spec.md` is normative — where
  a module README and its `spec.md` disagree, `spec.md` wins.

The desktop UI lives in sibling `desktop/` in this monorepo. When a JSON-RPC
contract, port, or push event changes, update the producing Go service, the
Electron bridge under `desktop/src/electron/service-bridge/`, and run
`npm --prefix desktop run service-contracts:check`.
